> Inspect the actual saved results

The figures below read actual saved outputs from this run. Native graph previews appear above the complete program. Reconstructed-task results retain the source budgets and are not reported as original benchmark scores.

> Actual validation history

Each panel reads the first recorded objective from a saved `history.tsv`. Different tasks and loss definitions have different units; compare curves within a panel. These are reconstructed-data outcomes with the original update budgets.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pointer_generator_history.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace fs=std::filesystem;std::vector<fs::path> files;for(const auto&entry:fs::recursive_directory_iterator("build/nn-completion/models/pointer_generator"))if(entry.path().filename()=="history.tsv")files.push_back(entry.path());std::sort(files.begin(),files.end());if(files.empty())throw std::runtime_error("actual validation histories missing");auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create((files.size()+1)/2,std::min(size_t(2),files.size()));for(const auto&file:files){std::ifstream in(file);std::string header,line;std::getline(in,header);std::vector<double>x,y;while(std::getline(in,line)){std::istringstream row(line);double step,value;if(row>>step>>value){x.push_back(step);y.push_back(value);}}if(x.empty())continue;auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,y,"saved validation objective",{37,99,235}).points(x,y,"saved rows",{37,99,235},4).x_label("Epoch or source step").y_label("Source objective; panels may use different units").title(file.parent_path().filename().string());layout.add(plot);}layout.size(1200,std::max(size_t(700),400*((files.size()+1)/2))).fit_panels().save_svg("build/pointer_generator_history.svg");}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/pointer_generator_history.svg)
// result_end


> Actual saved attention layout

This reads `copy/outputs.npz`, field `attention`, from the real held-out run. It shows the first leading-index slice and at most64 rows/columns. For sparse, hashed or projected attention, candidate slots are the source layout, not a dense physical-token axis. The complete program retains the index/projection mappings. Attention is not a saliency or causal explanation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pointer_generator_attention.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto load=[](const std::string&path){auto a=dm::nn::load_npz(path);return std::map<std::string,dm::nn::Tensor>(a.begin(),a.end());};auto a=load("build/nn-completion/models/pointer_generator/copy/outputs.npz");auto tensor=a.at("attention");int rows=tensor.size(tensor.dim()-2),columns=tensor.size(tensor.dim()-1),r=std::min(rows,64),c=std::min(columns,64);auto values=tensor.to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>x(c),y(r);std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);std::iota(y.begin(),y.end(),0.);std::vector<std::vector<double>>z(c,std::vector<double>(r));for(int i=0;i<r;++i)for(int j=0;j<c;++j)z[j][i]=values[i*columns+j];std::print("Native saved attention last axes: {} by {}; showing first sample/head/chunk and up to64 positions. Colour range: zero to the maximum in these rows, {}.\n",rows,columns,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.begin()+r*columns));dm::graphics::RPlot::create().image(x,y,z,dm::graphics::terrain_colors(256),0,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.begin()+r*columns)).title("pointer generator actual attention").x_label("Source key/candidate/compressed slot index").y_label("Source query/layout row index").size(1000,750).save_svg("build/pointer_generator_attention.svg");}
```
